{
  "_docs_1": "Defaults. Personal overrides go in config.local.json (gitignored) - any key there overrides the same key here WHOLESALE. The NTFY_TOPIC env var beats both (used by GitHub Actions secrets).",
  "_docs_2": "ATS slugs below were verified against live Summer2027 hardware postings (URL-mined from SimplifyJobs listings.json) and against zshah101's 4,054-board ATS registry. Slugs marked in _unverified_slugs are guesses - bad slugs only log a WARN and get skipped.",
  "_docs_3": "listings_repos roll over yearly (Summer2027 -> Summer2028). If one starts 404ing, check github.com/SimplifyJobs for the new repo name. Append :branch to override the default 'dev' branch.",
  "_docs_4": "Defense filtering is OFF (exclude_companies empty, no defense exclude_keywords, desc_clearance empty). Defense primes/labs sit in big_companies, so they push at default priority while startups push at high and sort first.",
  "_docs_5": "IMPLEMENTED in watch.py + worker.js: include_terms (season filter on listing.terms; rows lacking a terms field are kept), require_active, exclude_companies (company-level blocklist), markdown_sources, atom_feeds, and a Workday adapter. keep() already falls back to keyword-only for sources with no category (e.g. vanshb03), so that source was never contributing zero.",
  "_docs_6": "PAY GATE (watch.py extract_pay / cloudflare/filters.mjs extractPay): only fires when an hourly $ figure is actually stated in the description (GH/Lever/Ashby inline, or a fetched Workday/Simplify desc) - no pay stated is ambiguous and never drops, per the rails. pay_floor_hourly: hard drop below this (positive evidence of low pay). pay_preferred_hourly: at/above this, no penalty. Between floor and preferred, the role only reaches Tier A / high-priority if it's a strong hardware/robotics fit (score >= pay_midband_min_score in watch.py; an explicit include_keywords title hit as the closest JS-side proxy, since the worker has no ported scoring table) - otherwise it still delivers, just demoted to Tier B / low-priority.",

