  "_resume_fit_note": "Resume fit (fit.py / cloudflare/fit.mjs): [weight, regex] rows scored against a posting's DUTIES + QUALIFICATIONS only - the company blurb and benefits/EEO tail are dropped (their 'autonomous / robot / computer vision' boilerplate made web roles look like fits). Each row counts once. Built from the resume's DISTINCTIVE skills (embedded/RTOS, HIL/SIL, flight SW, ROS2/autonomy, edge ML, C++, sim/QEMU, CI test automation, bus protocols, wireless, Qt/LVGL, clearance) - not generic web stack, which every applicant has. A generic software/ML title at ANY company counts as relevant when fit >= resume_fit_min (curated boards: inline description, also enforced by the worker; Simplify/Workday/discovery: the description is fetched under fit_fetch_budget per run, cached, and the role is retried until fetched). Any role whose description clears the bar also scores +resume_fit_score. Weight-1 rows are GENERIC (C++, Linux, real-time, distributed systems...) and together add at most resume_fit_generic_cap, so a role needs >= 3 points of distinctive skills - a big-tech search/infra SWE listing 'C++, Linux, low-latency, distributed systems' does not qualify.",
  "resume_fit_min": 5,
  "_resume_fit_min_edge_note": "edge_companies no longer bypass the fit check (that let an ACS Android role through) - they get this lower bar instead. Measured: bypass = 12 good / 25 bad at edge companies; bar 2 + title check = 12 good / 1 bad (with Palantir off the edge list).",
  "resume_fit_min_edge": 2,
  "_specialty_titles_note": "A generic software title naming an off_specialty (Android, Frontend, Infrastructure...) is never rescued by fit or edge company - the title says what the work is, even when the description is full of the company's domain words. on_specialty overrides it ('Onboard Infrastructure', 'Vehicle Platforms').",
